From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Use wheel's build command when the setuptools module is absent
Source: https://github.com/JarryShaw/lorem/blob/04b9e25393906e45e1894b1c63a62e0224a370c7/setup.py
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
Upstream-Status: Not submitted; local compatibility for target setuptools 68
Root-Cause: setup.py imports setuptools.command.bdist_wheel unconditionally,
 although declared setuptools>=61 includes versions without that module.
Affected-Version: python-lorem 1.3.0.post3 with target setuptools 68.0.0
Remove-When: upstream handles the import or target setuptools provides it

The target's wheel 0.40.0 provides the bdist_wheel Command subclass and run
interface already used by lorem_bdist_wheel. Fall back only for the exact
missing setuptools module, not a dependency or arbitrary import failure.
This does not change library behavior, runtime tests, or coverage settings.

